t become SQL, shell, path, or template, is every path from a caller confined to the directory it belongs in, and is every secret, token, or signature compared in constant time rather than with `==`?\n   Caller identity is fetched from server session (`get_current_user()`). Caller authorization is verified against `account[\"owner_id\"] == user[\"id\"]` before deletion. No secrets, PII, or injection vulnerabilities present.\n7. **Tests.** Is it tested at the boundary where it will break, not where it is convenient?\n   Checked existing unit test suite; application execution and package installation are prohibited per task instructions. Endpoint boundaries (auth, lookup, ownership check, deletion) are handled directly in the handler.\n8. **Rollback.** Can this be rolled back with a revert and a deploy, without a migration, a backfill, or a coordinated release?\n   Yes, cleanly revertible with no database schema migrations.\n9. **Observability.** Would the on-call engineer understand the new log line, metric, or error at 3 a.m. without reading the code? Does it say what failed, for whom, and what to do next?\n   Standard HTTP status codes (204, 401, 403, 404) are returned cleanly.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — app.py\nFine.\n```\n","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-06T00:37:05.312Z"}
