ng rejects malformed and negative parameter boundaries with 400.\n\n8. **Rollback.** Can this be rolled back with a revert and a deploy?\nYes, standard code-only revert with no schema migrations or data backfill needed.\n\n9. **Observability.** Would the on-call engineer understand the new log line, metric, or error at 3 a.m.?\nReturns standard HTTP 400 on bad client parameters; no ambiguous internal error raised.\n\nGRUMP: APPROVE — /Users/sandeepbazar/.gemini/antigravity-cli/scratch/app.py\nFine.\n","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-06T00:41:32.884Z"}
