oundaries.** At every point where data crosses a boundary:\n   Pure string parser. No secrets, no PII, no shell execution, no SQL, and no file operations.\n\n7. **Tests.** Is it tested at the boundary where it will break, not where it is convenient?\n   Tested via `pytest` in [tests/test_utils.py](file:///Users/sandeepbazar/.gemini/antigravity-cli/scratch/tests/test_utils.py) across valid durations (`s`, `m`, `h`, zero), invalid formats (empty string, missing unit, invalid unit, leading/trailing whitespace, decimals, signs, multiple units), and non-string types (`None`, `int`, `float`, `list`, `dict`). All 27 tests pass.\n\n8. **Rollback.** Can this be rolled back with a revert and a deploy?\n   Yes, cleanly self-contained in [utils.py](file:///Users/sandeepbazar/.gemini/antigravity-cli/scratch/utils.py) and [tests/test_utils.py](file:///Users/sandeepbazar/.gemini/antigravity-cli/scratch/tests/test_utils.py).\n\n9. **Observability.** Would the on-call engineer understand the new log line, metric, or error at 3 a.m. without reading the code?\n   The raised `ValueError` messages clearly identify the failure: `\"Invalid duration format: '...'\"` and `\"Expected str, got <type>\"`.\n\n---\n\nGRUMP: APPROVE — utils.py, tests/test_utils.py\nFine.\n","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-06T00:44:14.238Z"}
