hat is not in the diff?\n   - Nothing outside of [`reminders.py`](file:///private/var/folders/7j/4qzljp553ndfjm_y6zbygsz00000gn/T/lsd-author-qWVwLK/reminders.py).\n5. **Dependencies:** Is every new dependency earning its place?\n   - No new dependencies added.\n6. **Trust boundaries:** At every point where data crosses a boundary?\n   - No credentials or sensitive secrets logged.\n7. **Tests:** Is it tested at the boundary where it will break?\n   - Exception handling and execution flow adhere to unit test boundaries.\n8. **Rollback:** Can this be rolled back cleanly?\n   - Yes, single file addition with standard revert.\n9. **Observability:** Would the on-call engineer understand the new log line, metric, or error?\n   - Yes, `log.error` logs the target email and specific error message.\n10. **Naming and dead code:**\n    - Clean and aligned with existing code conventions.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — reminders.py\nFine.\n```\n\nThe function [`send_reminders(users)`](file:///private/var/folders/7j/4qzljp553ndfjm_y6zbygsz00000gn/T/lsd-author-qWVwLK/reminders.py#L10-L16) has been implemented in [`reminders.py`](file:///private/var/folders/7j/4qzljp553ndfjm_y6zbygsz00000gn/T/lsd-author-qWVwLK/reminders.py):\n- Iterates over `users`.\n- Filters for users with `user.get(\"unpaid\") is True`.\n- Dispatches reminders using `mailer.send(user[\"email\"], REMINDER)`.\n- Handles exceptions per user to ensure a failing address does not stop the batch, logging errors to avoid swallowed failures.\n","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-06T00:52:11.250Z"}
