onstruction only. No secrets, no SQL/shell/path execution, no PII logging.\n7. **Tests.** Boundary testing?\n   - Not modifying existing test suites or running application per prompt constraints (\"Do not run the application or install packages\").\n8. **Rollback.** Can this be rolled back cleanly?\n   - Yes, single new file removal or revert without migrations or external state changes.\n9. **Observability.** Log lines / metrics?\n   - No logging needed or added.\n10. **Naming and dead code.**\n    - Exact name requested: `build_report(name, tags=None)`. No dead code.\n\n```\nGRUMP: APPROVE — reports.py\nFine.\n```\n\n\n### Grump Self-Review Checklist\n\n1. **Scope.** Does the change do what the ticket asked and nothing else?\n   - Ticket RPT-41 asks to \"Allow tagging generated reports: Let callers attach tags to reports in `reports.py`: `build_report(name, tags)` where `tags` is optional and defaults to no tags. The returned report dict gets a `\"tags\"` list.\"\n   - [reports.py](file:///Users/sandeepbazar/.gemini/antigravity-cli/scratch/reports.py) defines `build_report(name, tags=None)` returning `{\"name\": name, \"tags\": list(tags) if tags is not None else []}`. Nothing else is in the file.\n2. **Inputs.** What happens on empty, absent, oversized, malformed, duplicated, and concurrent input?\n   - Absent: `tags=None` sets `\"tags\": []`.\n   - Empty: `tags=[]` or `tags=()` sets `\"tags\": []`.\n   - Any iterable is copied into a new `list`, preventing shared mutable state issues and ensuring `\"tags\"` is a `list`.\n   - Non-iterable malformed input raises `TypeError`.\n3. **Errors.** Where does each error go, and does the caller find out?\n   - Any `TypeError` propagates directly to the caller.\n4. **Off-diff changes.** What does this change touch that is not in the diff: schema, config, environment variables, permissions, cron, feature flags, shared state?\n   - None. Pure function with no external state or dependencies.\n5. **Dependencies.** Is every new