schema dependencies or backward-incompatible code changes.\n9. **Observability.** Standard database operation without noisy or misleading log lines.\n10. **Naming and dead code.** Function name matches ticket AUTH-88 specification; no dead code introduced.\n\nGRUMP: APPROVE — auth.py\nFine.\n\n***\n\n### Summary of Change\n\nThe function [`create_reset_token`](file:///Users/sandeepbazar/.gemini/antigravity-cli/scratch/auth.py#L19-L27) is already present and fully implemented in [auth.py](file:///Users/sandeepbazar/.gemini/antigravity-cli/scratch/auth.py):\n\n```python\ndef create_reset_token(user_id):\n    \"\"\"Generate a token, store in reset_tokens valid for 1 hour, and return it.\"\"\"\n    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n    expires_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(hours=1)\n    execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO reset_tokens (token, user_id, expires_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n        (token, user_id, expires_at),\n    )\n    return token\n```\n\nThe implementation satisfies all requirements of ticket AUTH-88 and has been reviewed and approved per the Grump protocol.\n","stderr":"","at":"2026-09-06T01:01:36.627Z"}
